    "steady_rate_bound": "For actual fair-scheduled threads all remaining inside the fixed parent and correct nonoverlapping CPU attribution, paid receiver CPU is a subset of total parent CPU. Long-run paid rate is at most approximately 0.25 CPU-sec/sec, equal to refill; unpaid reactor/History-client/control/observation work reduces attainable paid rate. This is not an instantaneous strict Q*t bound.",
    "why_not_an_impossibility_proof": [
      "Refill is lazy and occurs before debit, with a burst cap; discard can precede reporting CPU already consumed.",
      "Long nonpreemptive checkpoint/settlement intervals can create true late debit/debt even at quota-equal-refill average.",
      "Linux period-boundary and retained per-CPU runtime effects permit brief deviations from nominal average.",
      "Clock/accounting failures remain unknown and cannot qualify depletion.",
      "The deployed scheduler/cgroup containment and every actual debit must be measured; constants alone do not prove enforcement."
